## Project identity
**Descriptive name:** **Sensor-Perception Learning Workspace — Udacity-Guided LiDAR Obstacle Detection + Python Radar Fundamentals**

Repository 027 is the strongest technical artifact in this six-repository batch and a major return to the autonomous-sensing thread first observed in Repo013.

It contains two distinct technical tracks:

### Track A — LiDAR

C++ / PCL obstacle detection derived from the **Udacity Sensor Fusion Self-Driving Car Course**.

### Track B — Radar

A large Jupyter notebook with numerical study of:

- radar waves;
- wavelength/radar equation;
- maximum range;
- FMCW range resolution;
- chirp bandwidth/time;
- beat-frequency range;
- Doppler velocity;
- FFT;
- 2D FFT.

No final implementation of:

- LiDAR/radar fusion;
- Kalman filtering;
- CFAR;
- Range-Doppler-map detection chain;
- real sensor acquisition

is observed.

Correct classification:

> **guided sensor-perception learning workspace**, not a production sensor-fusion stack.

